IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei2-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), ss 42 to 47: benefits cannot be assigned; liability to repay; the return of
-- benefits by claimants, employers and others; directors' liability for penalties; debts to the Crown. Piece ei2.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
-- Seat: the claimant (ss 42 to 45, 46(1)'s effect on the claimant's earnings, 46.01, 47). The employer's and the
-- director's provisions (ss 46(2), 46.1) are encoded here for what they decide and are not asked in the claimant's seat.
--
-- Relations (Hohfeld). s 42(1): the claimant's immunity from any assignment or charge of benefits (anyone's attempt is void: a
-- disability). ss 42(2) and (3): the Commission's power to recover or deduct; the claimant is liable to it. s 43: the claimant's
-- duty to repay, the Crown's claim. s 44: the person's duty to return, the Commission's claim. s 45: the claimant's duty
-- to pay the Receiver General. s 46(1) and (2): the employer's or other payer's duty to deduct and remit, the Receiver
-- General's claim; the claimant is liable to have earnings reduced. s 46.01: the employer's and claimant's immunity.
-- s 46.1: the directors' joint and several liability, the Crown's claim. s 47: the Crown's claim as a debt; its power to
-- deduct from benefits; the debtor's immunity after 72 months.
--
-- Amounts that depend on the Regulations' rules of earnings (what the benefits would have been had the earnings been paid in
-- time) are out of range (Regulations ss 35 to 39, piece er3) and are NUMBER inputs. A time limit of "n months" ends on the
-- n-month anniversary, which counts, and "more than n months have elapsed" is true from the day after it (fork ei2-F10).

§ `Section 42 - benefits not assignable; recovery and deduction`

-- (1): "Subject to subsections (2) and (3), benefits are not capable of being assigned, charged, attached, anticipated or
-- given as security and any transaction appearing to do so is void." MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE (void) for such a transaction;
-- NOTHING for anything else, about which the subsection says nothing.
-- src:877 | Benefits not assignable
-- src:878 | 42 (1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), benefits are not capable of being assigned, charged, attached, anticipated or given as security and any transaction appearing to do so is void.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 42(1) (src:877-878)
GIVEN `the transaction concerns benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction appears to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give the benefits as security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is a recovery under subsection 42(2) or a deduction under subsection 42(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 42(1) a transaction appearing to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give benefits as security is void` IS
    IF     `the transaction concerns benefits`
       AND `the transaction appears to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give the benefits as security`
       AND (NOT `the transaction is a recovery under subsection 42(2) or a deduction under subsection 42(3)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): "Any amounts payable under this Act by any person and required to be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating
-- Account may be recovered out of any benefits payable to that person, without affecting any other mode of recovery."
-- src:879 | Exception — recovery of amounts payable
-- src:880 | (2) Any amounts payable under this Act by any person and required to be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account may be recovered out of any benefits payable to that person, without affecting any other mode of recovery.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 42(2) (src:879-880)
GIVEN `the amount is payable under the Act by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is required to be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits are payable to that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 42(2) the amount may be recovered out of the benefits payable to the person` IF
        `the amount is payable under the Act by the person`
    AND `the amount is required to be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account`
    AND `benefits are payable to that person`

-- (3): "If the Government of Canada, a provincial or municipal government or any other prescribed authority pays a person an
-- advance or assistance or a welfare payment for a week that would not be paid if unemployment benefits were paid for that
-- week, and unemployment benefits subsequently become payable to that person for that week, the Commission may, subject
-- to the regulations, deduct from those or any subsequent benefits and pay to the government or the prescribed authority an
-- amount equal to the amount of the advance, assistance or welfare payment paid, if the person had, on or before
-- receiving the advance, assistance or welfare payment, consented to the deduction and payment by the Commission."
-- The regulations that limit it are reg 57 (out of range: Regulations s 57, piece er3).
-- src:881 | Exception — payment to other governments
-- src:882 | (3) If the Government of Canada, a provincial or municipal government or any other prescribed authority pays a person an advance or assistance or a welfare payment for a week that would not be paid if unemployment benefits were paid for that week, and unemployment benefits subsequently become payable to that person for that week, the Commission may, subject to the regulations, deduct from those or any subsequent benefits and pay to the government or the prescribed authority an amount equal to the amount of the advance, assistance or welfare payment paid, if the person had, on or before receiving the advance, assistance or welfare payment, consented to the deduction and payment by the Commission.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 42(3) (src:881-882)
GIVEN `the Government of Canada, a provincial or municipal government or any other prescribed authority pays the person an advance or assistance or a welfare payment for a week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment would not be paid if unemployment benefits were paid for that week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `unemployment benefits subsequently become payable to the person for that week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had, on or before receiving the payment, consented to the deduction and payment by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 42(3) the Commission may deduct from the benefits and pay to the government or authority` IF
        `the Government of Canada, a provincial or municipal government or any other prescribed authority pays the person an advance or assistance or a welfare payment for a week`
    AND `the payment would not be paid if unemployment benefits were paid for that week`
    AND `unemployment benefits subsequently become payable to the person for that week`
    AND `the person had, on or before receiving the payment, consented to the deduction and payment by the Commission`

-- src:881 | Exception — payment to other governments
-- src:882 | (3) If the Government of Canada, a provincial or municipal government or any other prescribed authority pays a person an advance or assistance or a welfare payment for a week that would not be paid if unemployment benefits were paid for that week, and unemployment benefits subsequently become payable to that person for that week, the Commission may, subject to the regulations, deduct from those or any subsequent benefits and pay to the government or the prescribed authority an amount equal to the amount of the advance, assistance or welfare payment paid, if the person had, on or before receiving the advance, assistance or welfare payment, consented to the deduction and payment by the Commission.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 42(3) (src:881-882)
GIVEN `the Commission may deduct from the benefits and pay to the government or authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the advance, assistance or welfare payment paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 42(3) the amount the Commission may deduct and pay` IS
    IF `the Commission may deduct from the benefits and pay to the government or authority`
    THEN JUST `the amount of the advance, assistance or welfare payment paid`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 43 to 45 - repayment of overpayments`

-- 43: "A claimant is liable to repay an amount paid by the Commission to the claimant as benefits (a) for any period for which
-- the claimant is disqualified; or (b) to which the claimant is not entitled."
-- src:883 | Liability for overpayments
-- src:884 | 43 A claimant is liable to repay an amount paid by the Commission to the claimant as benefits
-- src:885 | (a) for any period for which the claimant is disqualified; or
-- src:886 | (b) to which the claimant is not entitled.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 43 (src:883-886)
GIVEN `the amount was paid by the Commission to the claimant as benefits for a period for which the claimant is disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount was paid by the Commission to the claimant as benefits to which the claimant is not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 43 the claimant is liable to repay the amount` IF
       `the amount was paid by the Commission to the claimant as benefits for a period for which the claimant is disqualified`
    OR `the amount was paid by the Commission to the claimant as benefits to which the claimant is not entitled`

-- src:883 | Liability for overpayments
-- src:884 | 43 A claimant is liable to repay an amount paid by the Commission to the claimant as benefits
-- src:885 | (a) for any period for which the claimant is disqualified; or
-- src:886 | (b) to which the claimant is not entitled.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 43 (src:883-886)
GIVEN `the claimant is liable to repay the amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount paid by the Commission to the claimant as benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 43 the amount the claimant is liable to repay` IS
    IF `the claimant is liable to repay the amount`
    THEN `the amount paid by the Commission to the claimant as benefits`
    ELSE 0

-- 44: "A person who has received or obtained a benefit payment to which the person is disentitled, or a benefit payment in
-- excess of the amount to which the person is entitled, shall without delay return the amount, the excess amount or the
-- special warrant for payment of the amount, as the case may be." The text sets no time: "without delay" is a duty
-- whose timing is not computed.
-- src:887 | Liability to return overpayment
-- src:888 | 44 A person who has received or obtained a benefit payment to which the person is disentitled, or a benefit payment in excess of the amount to which the person is entitled, shall without delay return the amount, the excess amount or the special warrant for payment of the amount, as the case may be.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 44 (src:887-888)
GIVEN `the amount of a benefit payment received or obtained to which the person is disentitled` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount by which a benefit payment received or obtained exceeds the amount to which the person is entitled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 44 the amount the person shall return without delay` IS
    `the amount of a benefit payment received or obtained to which the person is disentitled` PLUS `the amount by which a benefit payment received or obtained exceeds the amount to which the person is entitled`

-- 45: "If a claimant receives benefits for a period and, under a labour arbitration award or court judgment, or for any other
-- reason, an employer, a trustee in bankruptcy or any other person subsequently becomes liable to pay earnings, including
-- damages for wrongful dismissal or proceeds realized from the property of a bankrupt, to the claimant for the same period
-- and pays the earnings, the claimant shall pay to the Receiver General as repayment of an overpayment of benefits an
-- amount equal to the benefits that would not have been paid if the earnings had been paid or payable at the time the
-- benefits were paid." Those benefits are worked out under the Regulations' rules of earnings (out of range: Regulations
-- ss 35 to 39, piece er3): the input. With any condition missing no amount is payable under s 45: 0.
-- src:889 | Return of benefits by claimant
-- src:890 | 45 If a claimant receives benefits for a period and, under a labour arbitration award or court judgment, or for any other reason, an employer, a trustee in bankruptcy or any other person subsequently becomes liable to pay earnings, including damages for wrongful dismissal or proceeds realized from the property of a bankrupt, to the claimant for the same period and pays the earnings, the claimant shall pay to the Receiver General as repayment of an overpayment of benefits an amount equal to the benefits that would not have been paid if the earnings had been paid or payable at the time the benefits were paid.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 45 (src:889-890)
GIVEN `the claimant receives benefits for a period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an employer, a trustee in bankruptcy or any other person subsequently becomes liable to pay earnings to the claimant for the same period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person pays the earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits that would not have been paid if the earnings had been paid or payable at the time the benefits were paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 45 the amount the claimant shall pay to the Receiver General` IS
    IF     `the claimant receives benefits for a period`
       AND `an employer, a trustee in bankruptcy or any other person subsequently becomes liable to pay earnings to the claimant for the same period`
       AND `that person pays the earnings`
    THEN `the benefits that would not have been paid if the earnings had been paid or payable at the time the benefits were paid`
    ELSE 0

§ `Section 46 - return of benefits by an employer or other person`

-- (1): "If under a labour arbitration award or court judgment, or for any other reason, an employer, a trustee in bankruptcy
-- or any other person becomes liable to pay earnings, including damages for wrongful dismissal or proceeds realized from the
-- property of a bankrupt, to a claimant for a period and has reason to believe that benefits have been paid to the claimant
-- for that period, the employer or other person shall ascertain whether an amount would be repayable under section 45 if
-- the earnings were paid to the claimant and if so shall deduct the amount from the earnings payable to the claimant and
-- remit it to the Receiver General as repayment of an overpayment of benefits."
-- src:891 | Return of benefits by employer or other person
-- src:892 | 46 (1) If under a labour arbitration award or court judgment, or for any other reason, an employer, a trustee in bankruptcy or any other person becomes liable to pay earnings, including damages for wrongful dismissal or proceeds realized from the property of a bankrupt, to a claimant for a period and has reason to believe that benefits have been paid to the claimant for that period, the employer or other person shall ascertain whether an amount would be repayable under section 45 if the earnings were paid to the claimant and if so shall deduct the amount from the earnings payable to the claimant and remit it to the Receiver General as repayment of an overpayment of benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 46(1) (src:891-892)
GIVEN `an employer, a trustee in bankruptcy or any other person becomes liable to pay earnings to the claimant for a period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person has reason to believe that benefits have been paid to the claimant for that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount that would be repayable under section 45 if the earnings were paid to the claimant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 46(1) the amount to deduct from the earnings payable to the claimant and remit to the Receiver General` IS
    IF     `an employer, a trustee in bankruptcy or any other person becomes liable to pay earnings to the claimant for a period`
       AND `that person has reason to believe that benefits have been paid to the claimant for that period`
    THEN `the amount that would be repayable under section 45 if the earnings were paid to the claimant`
    ELSE 0

-- (2): "If a claimant receives benefits for a period and under a labour arbitration award or court judgment, or for any other
-- reason, the liability of an employer to pay the claimant earnings, including damages for wrongful dismissal, for the same
-- period is or was reduced by the amount of the benefits or by a portion of them, the employer shall remit the amount or
-- portion to the Receiver General as repayment of an overpayment of benefits."
-- src:893 | Return of benefits by employer
-- src:894 | (2) If a claimant receives benefits for a period and under a labour arbitration award or court judgment, or for any other reason, the liability of an employer to pay the claimant earnings, including damages for wrongful dismissal, for the same period is or was reduced by the amount of the benefits or by a portion of them, the employer shall remit the amount or portion to the Receiver General as repayment of an overpayment of benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 46(2) (src:893-894)
GIVEN `the claimant receives benefits for a period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability of an employer to pay the claimant earnings for the same period is or was reduced by the amount of the benefits or by a portion of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount or portion by which the liability was reduced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 46(2) the amount the employer shall remit to the Receiver General` IS
    IF     `the claimant receives benefits for a period`
       AND `the liability of an employer to pay the claimant earnings for the same period is or was reduced by the amount of the benefits or by a portion of them`
    THEN `the amount or portion by which the liability was reduced`
    ELSE 0

-- 46.01: "No amount is payable under section 45, or deductible under subsection 46(1), as a repayment of an overpayment of
-- benefits if more than 36 months have elapsed since the lay-off or separation from the employment in relation to which the
-- earnings are paid or payable and, in the opinion of the Commission, the administrative costs of determining the repayment
-- would likely equal or exceed the amount of the repayment." More than 36 months have elapsed from the day after the
-- 36-month anniversary (fork ei2-F10); the opinion is the Commission's: a BOOLEAN input.
-- src:895 | Limitation
-- src:896 | 46.01 No amount is payable under section 45, or deductible under subsection 46(1), as a repayment of an overpayment of benefits if more than 36 months have elapsed since the lay-off or separation from the employment in relation to which the earnings are paid or payable and, in the opinion of the Commission, the administrative costs of determining the repayment would likely equal or exceed the amount of the repayment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 46.01 (src:895-896)
GIVEN `the day of the lay-off or separation from the employment` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the repayment would be determined` IS A DATE
      `in the opinion of the Commission the administrative costs of determining the repayment would likely equal or exceed the amount of the repayment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 46.01 no amount is payable under section 45 or deductible under subsection 46(1)` IF
        `the day on which the repayment would be determined` ABOVE (`add months` `the day of the lay-off or separation from the employment` 36)
    AND `in the opinion of the Commission the administrative costs of determining the repayment would likely equal or exceed the amount of the repayment`

§ `Section 46.1 - liability of directors to pay penalties`

-- (2)(a): "a certificate for the amount of the corporation's liability for the penalty has been registered in the Federal Court
-- under section 126 and execution for that amount has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part".
-- (2)(b): "the corporation has commenced liquidation or dissolution proceedings or has been dissolved and a claim for the amount
-- of its liability has been proved within six months after the date of commencement of the proceedings or the date of the
-- dissolution, whichever is earlier". (2)(c): "the corporation has made an assignment or a bankruptcy order has been made
-- against it under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act and a claim for the amount of its liability has been proved within six
-- months after the date of the assignment or bankruptcy order". Section 126 is piece ei4's.
-- src:899 | Limitations on liability
-- src:900 | (2) A director is not liable unless
-- src:901 | (a) a certificate for the amount of the corporation’s liability for the penalty has been registered in the Federal Court under section 126 and execution for that amount has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part;
-- src:902 | (b) the corporation has commenced liquidation or dissolution proceedings or has been dissolved and a claim for the amount of its liability has been proved within six months after the date of commencement of the proceedings or the date of the dissolution, whichever is earlier; or
-- src:903 | (c) the corporation has made an assignment or a bankruptcy order has been made against it under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act and a claim for the amount of its liability has been proved within six months after the date of the assignment or bankruptcy order.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 46.1(2) (src:899-903)
GIVEN `a certificate for the amount of the corporation's liability for the penalty has been registered in the Federal Court under section 126` IS A BOOLEAN
      `execution for that amount has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has commenced liquidation or dissolution proceedings or has been dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earlier of the date of commencement of the proceedings and the date of the dissolution` IS A DATE
      `the corporation has made an assignment or a bankruptcy order has been made against it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the assignment or bankruptcy order` IS A DATE
      `the day on which a claim for the amount of the corporation's liability was proved` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 46.1(2) a condition of the directors' liability is met` IF
        (   (`a certificate for the amount of the corporation's liability for the penalty has been registered in the Federal Court under section 126` AND `execution for that amount has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part`)
         OR (`the corporation has commenced liquidation or dissolution proceedings or has been dissolved` AND `a claim was proved by` `the day on which a claim for the amount of the corporation's liability was proved` `the earlier of the date of commencement of the proceedings and the date of the dissolution`)
         OR (`the corporation has made an assignment or a bankruptcy order has been made against it` AND `a claim was proved by` `the day on which a claim for the amount of the corporation's liability was proved` `the date of the assignment or bankruptcy order`))
    WHERE
        `a claim was proved by` provedOn eventDay MEANS
            CONSIDER provedOn
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST d  THEN d AT MOST (`add months` eventDay 6)

-- (3): "A director is not liable if the director exercised the degree of care, diligence and skill that a reasonably
-- prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances to prevent the act or omission for which the penalty is
-- imposed." The standard is a judgment: a BOOLEAN input.
-- src:904 | Defence of due diligence
-- src:905 | (3) A director is not liable if the director exercised the degree of care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances to prevent the act or omission for which the penalty is imposed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 46.1(3) (src:904-905)
GIVEN `the director exercised the degree of care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances to prevent the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 46.1(3) the director is not liable by reason of due diligence` IF
    `the director exercised the degree of care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances to prevent the act or omission`

-- (4): "No action or proceedings to recover any amount payable by a director shall be commenced more than six years after the
-- occurrence of the act or omission for which the penalty is imposed." The sixth anniversary counts (fork ei2-F10).
-- src:906 | Limitation period
-- src:907 | (4) No action or proceedings to recover any amount payable by a director shall be commenced more than six years after the occurrence of the act or omission for which the penalty is imposed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 46.1(4) (src:906-907)
GIVEN `the day on which the act or omission occurred` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the action or proceedings would be commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 46.1(4) the action or proceedings may be commenced` IF
    `the day on which the action or proceedings would be commenced` AT MOST (`add years` `the day on which the act or omission occurred` 6)

-- (1): "If a penalty is imposed on a corporation under section 38 or 39 for an act or omission, the directors of the
-- corporation at the time of the act or omission are, subject to subsections (2) to (7), jointly and severally, or
-- solidarily, liable, together with the corporation, to pay the amount of the penalty."
-- src:897 | Liability of directors to pay penalties
-- src:898 | 46.1 (1) If a penalty is imposed on a corporation under section 38 or 39 for an act or omission, the directors of the corporation at the time of the act or omission are, subject to subsections (2) to (7), jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable, together with the corporation, to pay the amount of the penalty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 46.1(1) (src:897-898)
GIVEN `a penalty is imposed on the corporation under section 38 or 39 for an act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a director of the corporation at the time of the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a condition of the directors' liability is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is not liable by reason of due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or proceedings may be commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 46.1(1) the director is jointly and severally liable, together with the corporation, to pay the penalty` IF
        `a penalty is imposed on the corporation under section 38 or 39 for an act or omission`
    AND `the person was a director of the corporation at the time of the act or omission`
    AND `a condition of the directors' liability is met`
    AND (NOT `the director is not liable by reason of due diligence`)
    AND `the action or proceedings may be commenced`

-- (5): "If execution referred to in paragraph (2)(a) has issued, the amount recoverable from a director is the amount remaining
-- unsatisfied after execution." NOTHING when execution has not issued: the subsection then fixes no amount.
-- src:908 | Amount recoverable
-- src:909 | (5) If execution referred to in paragraph (2)(a) has issued, the amount recoverable from a director is the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 46.1(5) (src:908-909)
GIVEN `execution referred to in paragraph 46.1(2)(a) has issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 46.1(5) the amount recoverable from a director` IS
    IF `execution referred to in paragraph 46.1(2)(a) has issued`
    THEN JUST `the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (6): "If a director pays an amount in respect of a corporation's liability that is proved in liquidation, dissolution or
-- bankruptcy proceedings, (a) the director is entitled to any preference that Her Majesty in right of Canada would have been
-- entitled to if that amount had not been paid; and (b) if a certificate that relates to that amount has been registered,
-- the director is entitled to an assignment of the certificate to the extent of the director's payment and the Commission
-- shall make the assignment." Two entitlements; the second needs a registered certificate.
-- src:910 | Preference
-- src:911 | (6) If a director pays an amount in respect of a corporation’s liability that is proved in liquidation, dissolution or bankruptcy proceedings,
-- src:912 | (a) the director is entitled to any preference that Her Majesty in right of Canada would have been entitled to if that amount had not been paid; and
-- src:913 | (b) if a certificate that relates to that amount has been registered, the director is entitled to an assignment of the certificate to the extent of the director’s payment and the Commission shall make the assignment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 46.1(6) (src:910-913)
GIVEN `a director pays an amount in respect of a corporation's liability that is proved in liquidation, dissolution or bankruptcy proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 46.1(6)(a) the director is entitled to any preference that Her Majesty in right of Canada would have been entitled to` IS
    IF `a director pays an amount in respect of a corporation's liability that is proved in liquidation, dissolution or bankruptcy proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:910 | Preference
-- src:911 | (6) If a director pays an amount in respect of a corporation’s liability that is proved in liquidation, dissolution or bankruptcy proceedings,
-- src:912 | (a) the director is entitled to any preference that Her Majesty in right of Canada would have been entitled to if that amount had not been paid; and
-- src:913 | (b) if a certificate that relates to that amount has been registered, the director is entitled to an assignment of the certificate to the extent of the director’s payment and the Commission shall make the assignment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 46.1(6)(b) (src:910-913)
GIVEN `a director pays an amount in respect of a corporation's liability that is proved in liquidation, dissolution or bankruptcy proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate that relates to that amount has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 46.1(6)(b) the director is entitled to an assignment of the certificate` IS
    IF     `a director pays an amount in respect of a corporation's liability that is proved in liquidation, dissolution or bankruptcy proceedings`
       AND `a certificate that relates to that amount has been registered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (7): "A director who has satisfied a claim under this section is entitled to contribution from the other directors who are
-- liable for the claim."
-- src:914 | Contribution from other directors
-- src:915 | (7) A director who has satisfied a claim under this section is entitled to contribution from the other directors who are liable for the claim.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 46.1(7) (src:914-915)
GIVEN `a director has satisfied a claim under section 46.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other director is liable for the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 46.1(7) the director is entitled to contribution from the other director` IS
    IF `a director has satisfied a claim under section 46.1` AND `the other director is liable for the claim`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 47 - debts to the Crown`

-- (1): "All amounts payable under section 38, 39, 43, 45, 46 or 46.1 are debts due to Her Majesty and are recoverable in the
-- Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by this Act."
-- src:916 | Debts to Crown
-- src:917 | 47 (1) All amounts payable under section 38, 39, 43, 45, 46 or 46.1 are debts due to Her Majesty and are recoverable in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 47(1) (src:916-917)
GIVEN `the amount is payable under section 38, 39, 43, 45, 46 or 46.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 47(1) the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty` IS
    IF `the amount is payable under section 38, 39, 43, 45, 46 or 46.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): "If benefits become payable to a claimant, the amount of the indebtedness may be deducted and retained out of the
-- benefits."
-- src:918 | Recovery
-- src:919 | (2) If benefits become payable to a claimant, the amount of the indebtedness may be deducted and retained out of the benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 47(2) (src:918-919)
GIVEN `the claimant owes an amount of indebtedness under subsection 47(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits become payable to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 47(2) the amount of the indebtedness may be deducted and retained out of the benefits` IF
        `the claimant owes an amount of indebtedness under subsection 47(1)`
    AND `benefits become payable to the claimant`

-- (3) and (4): "No amount due under this section may be recovered more than 72 months after the day on which the liability
-- arose." "A limitation period established by subsection (3) does not run when there is pending an appeal or other review of a
-- decision establishing the liability." The days on which an appeal or review was pending are left out of the count: the
-- last day to recover moves later by their number (fork ei2-F11). The day the liability arose can be fixed by s 52(3)(b)
-- (the day the Commission notifies the person of the amount).
-- src:920 | Limitation
-- src:921 | (3) No amount due under this section may be recovered more than 72 months after the day on which the liability arose.
-- src:922 | Appeals
-- src:923 | (4) A limitation period established by subsection (3) does not run when there is pending an appeal or other review of a decision establishing the liability.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 47(3), s 47(4) (src:920-923)
GIVEN `the day on which the liability arose` IS A DATE
      `the number of days within the 72 months during which an appeal or other review of a decision establishing the liability was pending` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which recovery would be attempted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 47(3) the amount may still be recovered` IF
    `the day on which recovery would be attempted` AT MOST ((`add months` `the day on which the liability arose` 72) PLUS `the number of days within the 72 months during which an appeal or other review of a decision establishing the liability was pending`)
